  "note": "Election of the whole Coleraine Borough Council under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946, polled Wednesday 16 October 1946 (not 18 September): five candidates for four aldermanic seats and thirteen for twelve councillorships; the results were declared on Thursday 17 October (Londonderry Sentinel, 19 October 1946, p. 6; Belfast News-Letter, 18 October 1946, p. 6). Nominations were received at the Town Hall on 1 October (Belfast News-Letter, 2 October 1946, p. 6). The queue's 18 September date is the Belfast county-borough poll; Coleraine polled later. Five candidates for four aldermanic seats. Seventy-five per cent. of the electorate of 3,532 voted. The outgoing Mayor, D. Hall Christie, topped the poll; R. F. M'Cartney, the oldest member and a recent freeman of the borough, was defeated. Sutherland is described as a former councillor. Murphy is a Labour candidate; Labour is the only label printed."
